{"id":"arnon","name":"Arnon","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:arnon"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Arnon","text":"Swift, the southern boundary of the territory of Israel beyond Jordan, separating it from the land of Moab (Deut. 3:8, 16). This river (referred to twenty-four times in the Bible) rises in the mountains of Gilead, and after a circuitous course of about 80 miles through a deep ravine it falls into the Dead Sea nearly opposite Engedi. The stream is almost dry in summer. It is now called el-Mujeb. The territory of the Amorites extended from the Arnon to the Jabbok."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H769","lemma":"אַרְנוֹן","xlit":"ʼArnôwn","gloss":"the Arnon, a river east of the Jordan, also its territor","kjv":"Arnon","count":10,"share":1},{"strong":"H5158","lemma":"נַחַל","xlit":"nachal","gloss":"a stream, especially a winter torrent","kjv":"brook, flood, river, stream","count":6,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H567","lemma":"אֱמֹרִי","xlit":"ʼĔmôrîy","gloss":"an Emorite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Amorite","count":4,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","xlit":"Môwʼâb","gloss":"Moab, an incestuous son of Lot","kjv":"Moab","count":4,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H5676","lemma":"עֵבֶר","xlit":"ʻêber","gloss":"a region across","kjv":"against, beyond, by, from","count":3,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H2768","lemma":"חֶרְמוֹן","xlit":"Chermôwn","gloss":"Chermon, a mount of Palestine","kjv":"Hermon","count":2,"share":0.2}],"verses":["Num.21.13","Num.21.14","Num.21.26","Num.22.36","Deut.2.24","Deut.2.36","Deut.3.8","Deut.3.16","Josh.12.1","Isa.16.2"],"related":[{"id":"sihon","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.121,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"rivers","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.031,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"moabites","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.022,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"amorites","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.021,"why":"4